   "x": 60,
   "y": 60,
   "text": "Example: Ethernet link – a PC (ETH1) and a switch port (ETH2) over a 30 m CAT6 cable with two RJ45 plugs",
   "size": 18,
   "bold": 1,
   "it": 0,
   "al": "left",
   "rot": 0
  },
  {
   "id": 202,
   "k": "text",
   "pg": 1,
   "all": 0,
   "col": "",
   "wd": 2,
   "ds": "",
   "x": 60,
   "y": 78,
   "text": "Press Run: the link LED turns green and shows the speed (1 Gbps). The cable shows its 4 twisted pairs and moving pulses.",
   "size": 12,
   "bold": 0,
   "it": 0,
   "al": "left",
   "rot": 0
  },
  {
   "id": 203,
   "k": "text",
   "pg": 1,
   "all": 0,
   "col": "",
   "wd": 2,
   "ds": "",
   "x": 60,
   "y": 96,
   "text": "Chain: device LAN → RJ45 PORT … RJ45 CABLE → cable A … B → RJ45 CABLE … RJ45 PORT → device LAN. Both plugs are T568B and the cable is straight-through: PC (MDI) to switch (MDI-X).",
   "size": 12,
   "bold": 0,
   "it": 0,
   "al": "left",
   "rot": 0
  },
  {
   "id": 204,
   "k": "text",
   "pg": 1,
   "all": 0,
   "col": "",
   "wd": 2,
   "ds": "",
   "x": 60,
   "y": 114,
   "text": "Break it: set a plug to Custom and swap two pins; set RJ1 to T568A (crossover!); make the cable 120 m; choose Crossover (with Auto MDI-X OFF); unshielded CAT5e with noise High; 10 Gbps over CAT6 beyond 55 m.",
   "size": 12,
